{"name":"Cowbell","hex":"#ffe481","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cowbell","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bell worn by cows; sometimes with an ornate strap.","A musical instrument, typically found without a clapper."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cowbell"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cowbell","blocks":[{"text":"A cowbell is a bell worn around the neck of free-roaming livestock so herders can keep track of an animal via the sound of the bell when the animal is grazing out of view in hilly landscapes or vast plains. Although they are typically referred to as \"cow bells\" due to their extensive use with cattle, the bells are used on a wide variety of animals."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Do-Bells-Affect-Behaviour-and-Heart-Rate-Variability-in-Grazing-Dairy-Cows-pone.0131632.s006.ogv/330px--Do-Bells-Affect-Behaviour-and-Heart-Rate-Variability-in-Grazing-Dairy-Cows-pone.0131632.s006.ogv.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cowbell","wikidata":"Q1236988"},{"title":"Cowbell (instrument)","blocks":[{"text":"The cowbell is an idiophone hand percussion instrument used in various styles of music, such as Latin and rock. It is named after the similar bell used by herdsmen to keep track of the whereabouts of cows. The instrument initially and traditionally has been metallic; however, contemporarily, some variants are made of synthetic materials."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/46/Koebel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cowbell_(instrument)","wikidata":"Q775570"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Azpigorriak_7.JPG/500px-Azpigorriak_7.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Azpigorriak_7.JPG/1280px-Azpigorriak_7.JPG?utm_source=en.